Replace this entire file's contents with the real Ampache API key (a single line, no
trailing newline needed) for the dedicated `wordpress_integration` Ampache user - see
plans/wordpress-ampache-plugin/03-security-privacy.md "Ampache account and ACL".

Steps:
1. In Ampache, create the level-25 user (e.g. `wordpress_integration`) and generate its API key.
2. Save the real key to /opt/wordpress/secrets/jba-ampache-api-key on the server (600, owned by
   the user that runs podman-compose - never committed).
3. Remove this placeholder text; the file should contain only the key itself.
4. Recreate the wordpress container (`sudo systemctl restart wordpress`) so it picks up the
   new bind mount.
